---
/**
 * THE SITE FRAME.
 *
 * Four fixed rails in the frame colour, plus four SVG fillets that round the
 * inside corners. The effect is that the whole viewport is a mount and the
 * page is a specimen sitting in it — which is the reference template's
 * signature device, and the reason a page composed of ordinary sections still
 * reads as one designed object.
 *
 * Everything here is `pointer-events: none` and `aria-hidden`: it is a border,
 * not content. The floating header sits exactly on the top rail and grows its
 * own two fillets sideways into it, so the header appears cut from the same
 * sheet — see Header.astro.
 *
 * Hidden below 850px (in global.css, not here) where a 10px rail is only a
 * bezel eating the viewport, and hidden in print.
 *
 * Z-ORDER, declared once so nothing has to guess:
 *   130  skip link           — must clear everything, including the frame
 *   120  site frame rails
 *   119  frame corner fillets
 *   110  mobile menu sheet   — over the header, under the frame
 *    60  floating header
 *    10  in-page sticky bits (sticky table headers, sticky rails)
 */
---

<div class="site-frame site-frame-t" aria-hidden="true"></div>
<div class="site-frame site-frame-b" aria-hidden="true"></div>
<div class="site-frame site-frame-l" aria-hidden="true"></div>
<div class="site-frame site-frame-r" aria-hidden="true"></div>

{
  (["tl", "tr", "bl", "br"] as const).map((corner) => (
    <svg
      class={`site-corner site-corner-${corner}`}
      width="50"
      height="50"
      viewBox="0 0 50 50"
      fill="none"
      aria-hidden="true"
    >
      <path
        d="M5.50871e-06 0C-0.00788227 37.3001 8.99616 50.0116 50 50H5.50871e-06V0Z"
        fill="currentColor"
      />
    </svg>
  ))
}
